ass="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Add an interview day</b>: the day, from and to (Toronto time), the call length (15 minutes) and the break between calls (5 minutes), phone or video, and the roles it is for (empty: every role).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Phone: you call the candidate on the number they gave. Video: every booking gets its own Jitsi Meet link, in the candidate&#39;s email and on their page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Candidates book, move or cancel from their link. They get a confirmation, a reminder the evening before and one an hour before (and a text, when phone and texts are on). Remote roles show Manila time too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Turn off</b> stops new bookings on a day; a day with bookings cannot be deleted.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="hiring-run-the-calls-with-the-rubric" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Run the calls with the rubric</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Hiring</b>, tab Calls.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Pick the day. Each call shows the time, the candidate, Call (or the video link). Press <b class="gd-ui">Start</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">The rubric sits beside the call guide (what to ask each minute, and what a good answer sounds like). Score each line 1 to 5: Communication, Reliability and availability, Role skills, Customer or sales instinct, Judgement on the scenarios, Attitude.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the decision (Hire, Maybe, No, No show), add notes and press <b class="gd-ui">Save the rubric